# __PLUGIN_NAME__ — a Valuz App Plugin

This directory is a **Valuz App Plugin** (`__PLUGIN_ID__`). Valuz loads
its frontend bundle into the desktop app and gives it a restricted context: it
can add buttons, cards, tabs and pages in public places of the UI, and use
Valuz's own backend (projects, artifacts, knowledge, conversations, connector
tools, code automations, storage). It has no backend of its own.

Agent Plugins bundle skills and MCP connectors and use `valuz plugin agent …`; this App Plugin uses `valuz plugin app …`.

## Layout

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `valuz-plugin.json` | Manifest: id, version, names, permissions, config, automations (schema in `$schema`) |
| `src/index.tsx` | Source entry: `export default definePlugin({ id, apply(ctx) { … } })` |
| `src/*.css` | Optional CSS, imported from the source; scoped to the plugin by the build |
| `locales/<lang>.json` | The plugin's texts (`zh-CN.json`, `en-US.json`, same keys) |
| `test/*.test.tsx` | Tests (`node:test` + `@valuz/plugin-sdk/testing`) |
| `frontend/` | Build output (`index.js`, `index.css`) — never edit by hand |
| `automations/` | Scripts of code automations declared in the manifest |

## Commands

`valuz-plugin` is the SDK's command (if it is not on PATH: `node __SDK_BIN__`).

| Command | Does |
|---|---|
| `valuz-plugin build` | Bundle `src/` into `frontend/index.js` (+ `index.css`) |
| `valuz-plugin dev` | Build in watch mode and link this directory into the running Valuz (`--backend URL`) |
| `valuz-plugin test` | Run `test/**/*.test.tsx` (no Valuz needed) |
| `valuz-plugin validate` | Check the manifest, files and the built bundle |
| `valuz-plugin pack` | Validate and zip into `dist/<id>-<version>.zip` (prints the sha256) |

Install into Valuz: `valuz-plugin dev` (watch + link), or `valuz plugin app dev <dir>`
(link only; Valuz picks up every later `valuz-plugin build` by itself), or
`valuz-plugin pack` then `valuz plugin app install dist/<zip>`.
Check it with `valuz plugin app status __PLUGIN_ID__` / `valuz plugin app logs __PLUGIN_ID__`.

After every change run `valuz-plugin test` and `valuz-plugin validate`. Tests
passing is not "done": the developer confirms the UI inside Valuz.

## Rules

1. Import only `react`, `react-dom`, `@valuz/plugin-sdk` and
   `@valuz/plugin-sdk/ui` from the host. Never import `@valuz/core`,
   `@valuz/app`, `@valuz/ui` or other internal packages (not available at
   runtime; the build fails). Other npm packages are bundled into the plugin.
2. Ids you register are local (`"hello"`); Valuz namespaces them as
   `x:__PLUGIN_ID__:hello`. Register only into the 12 public slots below, add
   pages / settings sections / sidebar items — never remove or replace Valuz's own.
3. Page paths must be `/x/__PLUGIN_ID__` or below it.
4. `permissions` in `valuz-plugin.json` must list every capability the code
   uses through `ctx.valuz` / `useValuz()` (table below). A missing permission
   is a 403 at runtime.
5. No network calls of your own (`fetch`, websockets, analytics): data comes
   through `ctx.valuz` (a customer system is added as a connector and called with
   `valuz.connectors.callTool`); computation runs as a code automation.
6. Every user-facing text goes through `useTranslation()`; add each key to both
   `locales/zh-CN.json` and `locales/en-US.json`. Placeholders are `{{name}}`.
7. Style with the SDK's UI components; own CSS uses the host's CSS variables
   (`var(--color-ink-heading)`, `var(--color-primary)`, … — `tokens` in
   `@valuz/plugin-sdk/ui`) so light / dark themes work. Host Tailwind classes the
   host does not use itself do not work.
8. `definePlugin({ id })` must equal the manifest `id`. Bump `version` (SemVer)
   for every release.

## Registering UI (`apply(ctx)`)

```tsx
ctx.registry.slot("project.detail.tabs", { id: "board", key: "board", label: "board.title", component: slotComponent(Board) });
pageRoute(ctx, { id: "home", path: "/x/__PLUGIN_ID__", title: "home.title", icon: "plugins" }, HomePage, { nav: true });
settingsPage(ctx, { id: "settings", title: "settings.title" }, SettingsSection);
sidebarItem(ctx, { id: "home-link", label: "home.title", icon: "plugins", path: "/x/__PLUGIN_ID__" });
ctx.effect(() => { const timer = setInterval(tick, 60_000); return () => clearInterval(timer); });
```

Sidebar icon ids: assistant, knowledge, skills, scheduled, playbooks, activity, settings, agents, connectors, plugins, marketplace, projectTasks, star, compass, watchlist, portfolio, dashboard, globe (unknown ids show a gear).


`title` / `label` are keys of your locales (or plain text). Slot components get
the slot's props: type them as `SlotProps<"slot.name">`.

### The 12 public slots

| Slot | Kind | Props |
|---|---|---|
| `conversation.title.actions` | list | `sessionId`, `session`, `scrollToTop`, `turns` |
| `conversation.header.badges` | list | `sessionId`, `session`, `project`, `agentSlug` |
| `conversation.turn.actions` | list | `turn`, `scrollToTurn` |
| `conversation.tool-card.{tool}` | list | `tool`, `toolUseId`, `status`, `input`, `output`, `thinking`, `hostRef` |
| `conversation.composer.plus.menu-items` | list | `sessionId`, `projectId`, `setDraft`, `surface` |
| `conversation.empty.extra` | list | `projectId`, `agentSlug`, `setDraft` |
| `context-panel.tabs` | keyed (`key` required) | `projectId`, `sessionId`, `surface` |
| `project.detail.tabs` | keyed (`key` required) | `projectId`, `navigate` |
| `project.detail.header.actions` | list | `projectId`, `project`, `navigate` |
| `resource.{type}.actions` | list | `resourceType`, `resource` |
| `shell.topbar.actions` | list | `pathname`, `activeProjectId`, `rightPanelCollapsed` |
| `task.detail.sections` | list | `task`, `isCompleted` |

`session`, `project`, `turn`, `task`, `resource`, `tool` are the SDK's public
types (`PublicSession`, `PublicProject`, `PublicTurn`, `PublicTask`,
`PublicResource`, `PublicToolCall`). `conversation.tool-card.{tool}` replaces
the generic card of the tool named `{tool}` (e.g. an MCP tool of your connector).

## React hooks and host actions

| Hook | Returns |
|---|---|
| `useTranslation()` | `{ t, locale }` — `t(key, params?)` over your locales |
| `useValuz()` | the `ctx.valuz` client |
| `usePluginConfig()` | the plugin's config values (re-renders on change) |
| `useHostContext()` | `{ locale, theme, edition, deployment, orgId }` |

`host.navigate(path)`, `host.openSession(id)`, `host.openProject(id)`,
`host.toast({ title, description?, variant? })`,
`host.confirm({ title, body?, confirmLabel? })` → `Promise<boolean>`,
`host.openExternal(url)` (http(s) only), `host.copyText(text)`,
`host.draftConversation({ projectId?, agent?, text })`.

UI components (`@valuz/plugin-sdk/ui`, with their parts — `CardHeader`,
`DialogContent`, `TabsList` …): Button, Input, Textarea, Select, Checkbox,
Switch, Tabs, Table, Card, Badge, Dialog, Popover, Tooltip, DropdownMenu,
Skeleton, Spinner, LoadingState, Empty / EmptyState, ChartContainer /
ChartTooltip / ChartLegend, and `tokens` (the CSS variables).

## `ctx.valuz` (and `useValuz()`)

Errors are `ValuzApiError { status, code, message }`.

| Method | Permission |
|---|---|
| `projects.list()`, `projects.get(id)`, `projects.files(id, { path?, depth? })` | `projects:read` |
| `artifacts.list({ projectId?, sessionId? })`, `artifacts.content(revisionId)` | `artifacts:read` |
| `knowledge.search(query, { projectId?, kbIds?, topK? })`, `knowledge.get(docId)` | `knowledge:read` |
| `conversations.draft({ projectId?, agent?, text })` — opens a new conversation, the user sends | — |
| `conversations.send({ sessionId?, projectId?, agent?, text })` (experimental) | `conversations:write` |
| `conversations.events(sessionId, { afterSeq? })` | `conversations:read` |
| `connectors.list()`, `connectors.listTools(connector)` | `connectors:read` |
| `connectors.callTool(connector, tool, args)` — read-only tools | `connectors:call` |
| `connectors.callTool(connector, tool, args, { write: true })` — the user confirms (experimental) | `connectors:write` |
| `automations.run(name, input)`, `getRun(runId)`, `waitRun(runId, { timeoutMs? })`, `latestRun(name)` | `automations:run` |
| `storage.get(key)`, `set(key, value)`, `delete(key)`, `list(prefix?)` | `storage` |
| `notifications.post({ title, body?, link? })` (experimental) | `notifications` |

## Config, storage, automations

- **Config**: declare `"config"` in the manifest as a JSON Schema
  (`{"type": "object", "properties": {…}}`); Valuz renders the form in
  Settings → Plugins; read it with `usePluginConfig()` / `ctx.config`.
- **Storage**: per user × plugin JSON key-value store (key ≤ 200 chars, value
  ≤ 256 KiB, 10 MiB total), on this device only.
- **Automations**: computation runs as a code automation the manifest declares;
  Valuz creates it at install and deletes it at uninstall:

  ```json
  "automations": [
    { "name": "daily-summary", "runtime": "python", "entry": "automations/daily_summary.py",
      "input": { "type": "object", "properties": { "projectId": { "type": "string" } } },
      "result": "artifact", "timeoutSec": 300, "trigger": { "cron": "0 8 * * 1-5" } }
  ]
  ```

  Trigger it with `valuz.automations.run("daily-summary", { projectId })` and read
  the result with `waitRun` / `latestRun` (needs `automations:run`).

  A `python` script defines `run(ctx)`: `ctx["input"]` is the run input (matching
  `input`), `ctx["trigger"]["type"]` says how it started; it returns
  `{"artifact": {...}}` — that object is the run's output (`run.output`).
  Valuz runs it with the bundled `valuz-python` (standard library plus the
  bundled skills' packages; no `pip install`):

  ```python
  def run(ctx):
      project_id = (ctx.get("input") or {}).get("projectId")
      return {"artifact": {"projectId": project_id, "summary": "…"}}
  ```

## Testing

```tsx
import { createTestHost, mockValuz } from "@valuz/plugin-sdk/testing";
const host = createTestHost({ locales, valuz: mockValuz({ projects: [...], connectors: { "acme-data": { get_positions: () => ({ positions: [] }) } } }) });
await host.load(plugin, { permissions: manifest.permissions, locales });
host.capture().slots["conversation.title.actions"]; // ["x:__PLUGIN_ID__:hello"]
host.renderSlot("conversation.title.actions", props); // static HTML
host.renderRoute("/x/__PLUGIN_ID__/projects");
host.calls.toast; // what the plugin asked the host to do
```

`renderSlot` / `renderRoute` render static markup (effects do not run).
